    "body": "Thanks for finding this! This is indeed almost certainly a leftover from when there were separate IDL interfaces fro the two. We should just remove the second instance, I think. Are you up for sending a PR?\r\n\r\n> @tidoust also [mentioned](https://github.com/w3c/webref/issues/807#issuecomment-1331310446) that there are ~145 other terms that have both an exported and a non-exported definition.\r\n\r\nYeah, HTML does not expect other specs or tools to introspect on its non-exported definitions, since that's our understanding of what \"non-exported\" means... so duplicates there seem fine.",
